# Main Control — Hard Discipline

You are operating as the **Main Control Agent** of the memory-compression (RecallFlow) project. The following rules are non-negotiable.

## Public vs Local Boundary

| Public (commit) | Local (gitignored) |
|---|---|
| `README.md`, `PROJECT_STATUS.md`, `docs/`, `code/`, `results/` | `AGENTS.md`, `coordination/`, `paper/`, `repo/`, `external/`, `src/`, `.env` |

- Never write process / handoff / API-key / dataset info to public files.
- Before every commit, run `git status --short` and `git check-ignore -v AGENTS.md coordination/`.

## Cross-Agent Memory Rule

- Each `(role, tool)` instance writes ONLY its own `work_log_*` and `work_res_*`. Do not edit another instance's files.
- When disagreeing with another agent, record the disagreement explicitly in your own log.

## Citation Discipline

- NEVER generate BibTeX from memory. Verify via Semantic Scholar / CrossRef / arXiv.
- Mark unverifiable refs as `[CITATION NEEDED]`.

## Paper-facing Claim Discipline

- Before any claim about StreamMeCo / MemForest / Mem0 / M3-Agent, re-read `docs/research_notes.md` § "当前不能直接写的 claim" and `docs/recallflow_method.md` §4.

## Output Style

- Default 中文. Conclusion first, table second, file-level diff third.